Results and discussion
The optimal combination of data for integration
An overarching challenge to integrate multi-omics data lies in effectively incorporating diverse data types to generate biologically interpretable embeddings. To ensure effective data integration of scRNA-seq data, bulk proteomics and metabolomics, and molecular networks, we investigate which combination of the input data results in gene embeddings that best capture the molecular mechanisms associated with PD. Thus, we perform a grid search of the weighting factors
